<!--
  librdkafka settings for every Kafka engine table. These are NOT the kafka_*
  table settings (those live in the DDL, stream/clickhouse/sql/); this is the
  underlying client config.

  auto_offset_reset is the one that matters, and it is not the one you would
  guess. librdkafka defaults to "largest", i.e. latest, so a brand new consumer
  group starts at the end of the topic and silently skips everything already
  there. The first run of `make ch-tables` against a topic with a backlog would
  land none of it, and the verification step that compares row count against
  produced count would report what looks exactly like data loss.

  Flink's equivalent is 'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset' in
  stream/flink/jobs/*.sql. Same intent, same reason, different layer.

  (XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen, so no em dashes in this file.)
-->
<clickhouse>
    <kafka>
        <auto_offset_reset>earliest</auto_offset_reset>
    </kafka>
</clickhouse>
